 "text": "Hey, nice to hear from you. How are you? Try getting up every hour to stretch and move around. A standing desk is great too. shorter your sitting sessions, the less back pain. You can use a foot rest or raise the desk with drawers that pop out. Not necessarily, but a little forward bend in chair back can help. A straight back puts too much pressure on the lower back. Try taking short walking breaks every twenty minutes. It helps with energy too. If you sit for long periods, your butt muscles get really tight, and that pulls your whole body out of alignment.",
